{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/195","id":4589471170,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQmfsR88AAAABEY3Fwg","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/195","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/195.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pull/195.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/195","number":195,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix protected release PR checks and pin Ubuntu 24.04","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- make ruleset fallback pull requests use a dedicated `RELEASE_PR_TOKEN`, so their `pull_request` workflows actually run\n- wait for the fallback PR's own checks with `gh pr checks --watch --fail-fast` before merging\n- retry only GitHub's short check-discovery and mergeability races; fail immediately for failed checks, authentication errors, and repository-policy failures\n- pin every active Linux workflow job to `ubuntu-24.04`\n- document fine-grained PAT and GitHub App token setup, and add a patch changeset\n\n## Root cause and solution\n\n### Protected release pull requests (#192)\n\nThe existing fallback opened PRs with the workflow's built-in `GITHUB_TOKEN`. GitHub does not create new workflow runs for most events caused by that token, so a required `Pipeline Status` check could never appear and the fallback PR could not merge. Dispatching another workflow would not solve this: a `workflow_dispatch` check suite is not associated with the pull request and cannot satisfy its required PR check.\n\nThe fallback now fails closed unless `RELEASE_PR_TOKEN` is configured, uses that credential for all `gh pr` operations, waits for the PR-associated checks, and only then merges. The check wait retries the brief “no checks reported” discovery race. Merge retries are limited to the known mergeability-computation race, so permanent failures are returned without ten identical attempts.\n\nThe same dedicated credential is wired into release/version automation, manual changeset PR creation, and the example-app preview fallback. The preview commit no longer includes `[skip ci]`, because required checks must run on its fallback PR.\n\nRepository setup is documented in the README and best-practices guide. A fine-grained PAT needs repository `Contents: read and write`, `Pull requests: read and write`, and `Checks: read`; a short-lived GitHub App installation token with equivalent permissions is also supported.\n\n### Ubuntu runner pinning (#193)\n\nAll 33 active `ubuntu-latest` references across the five workflow files are pinned to `ubuntu-24.04`. A repository-wide workflow regression test rejects any future active `ubuntu-latest` reference. Existing macOS, Windows, and ARM labels remain unchanged.\n\n## Reproduction and verification\n\nThe regression tests reproduce the former deadlock by asserting that a failed/missing PR check prevents any merge call, that token absence prevents even the temporary branch push, and that the dedicated token is used for PR creation, check waiting, and merging. They also verify command ordering, transient-only retries, and all active workflow runner labels.\n\nLocal verification:\n\n- `npm run check`\n- `npm test` — 471 passed\n- `bun test --timeout 30000` — 471 passed\n- `deno test --allow-read` — 372 passed\n- example app production build\n- actionlint 1.7.12 in the repository's pinned Docker image\n- shell/MJS syntax, line-limit, and `git diff --check`\n\n## Alternatives researched\n\n- GitHub's native `gh pr checks` and `gh pr merge` remain sufficient; no third-party merge dependency is needed.\n- `actions/create-github-app-token` is the supported GitHub-owned option for generating a short-lived installation token before invoking these scripts.\n- Merge queue could also coordinate required checks, but would require repository-policy and workflow-trigger changes beyond this issue.\n- Versioned runner labels are intentionally used to avoid an unplanned `ubuntu-latest` image migration.\n\nFixes #194\n\nFixes #192\n\nFixes #193\n","created_at":"2026-09-21T08:31:03Z","updated_at":"2026-09-21T08:56:41Z","closed_at":"2026-09-21T08:56:40Z","merged_at":"2026-09-21T08:56:39Z","merge_commit_sha":"f2cd4d8623557241fa4127a57a77461751a2f734","assignees":[{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/195/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/195/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/issues/195/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template/statuses/1f5be7344f5476512cfe1aa98b145b29766888f7","head":{"label":"link-foundation:issue-194-1b92d4ad5049","ref":"issue-194-1b92d4ad5049","sha":"1f5be7344f5476512cfe1aa98b145b29766888f7","user":{"login":"link-foundation","id":176174013,"node_id":"O_kgDOCoAzvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176174013?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation","html_url":"https://github.com/link-foundation","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/link-foundation/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/